<%# The pools that belong to no account. Local: `presenter` (HomePresenter).

    A group of their own, because HomePresenter#pools_for filters on account_id: a band
    built purely as "for each account, render its pools" renders these NOWHERE. The heading
    is what they are, said once, so the rows below can speak the same §4.4 vocabulary as
    every other row.

    THIS PARTIAL RENDERS FOR NOBODY, and the sentence that used to be here — "an
    account-less savings pool is the ordinary shape until Plan 3's backfill, not a rare
    edge" — is out of date rather than merely optimistic: the backfill has run, every pool
    names an account, and a CHECK constraint refuses a new one. `presenter.orphan_pools`
    is empty for every user, so the `if` below is always false. Kept until the follow-up
    that deletes the apparatus whole; Pool::REFUSALS carries that list, and this file is
    on it.

    Silent when there are none: an empty "No account" heading invents a problem out of a
    healthy screen (principle 3). %>
<% pools = presenter.orphan_pools %>
<% if pools.any? %>
  <section class="bg-white border border-status-danger rounded" data-pool-group="No account">
    <div class="px-6 py-3 border-b border-gray-200 bg-status-danger-light flex justify-between items-baseline gap-4">
      <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-status-danger">No account</h3>
      <%# Not a shortfall and not a buffer — the money these ask for may be sitting in
          Checking right now with nowhere to go. Money does not fix this one; assigning
          the pool does, which is why the line says that instead of naming a figure. %>
      <span class="text-sm text-status-danger">nothing can fund these until you assign one</span>
    </div>

    <% pools.each do |pool| %>
      <%= render "pool_row", pool: pool, presenter: presenter, orphan: true %>
    <% end %>
  </section>
<% end %>
